From: UniXNU PR #249 (CrossDarwin), adapted to selected xnu-12377 series
Subject: Native 4 KiB bootstrap pool for owned windows up to 9 GiB

Source: UniXNU/UniXNU PR #249 @ 9b9db9c9ff13a595492d241366426383c88bf236
The selected xnu-12377 patch already introduces the guarded 16-page pool.
Apply the PR's 22-page budget after that official patch, without editing it.
This changes only the non-Apple 4 KiB branch; it is not a claimed fix for
an observed post-MMU arm_vm_init stop.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.h b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.h
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.h
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.h
@@ -118,9 +118,9 @@
 #define BOOTSTRAP_TABLE_SIZE (ARM_PGBYTES * 34)
 #elif !defined(APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY) && !__ARM_16K_PG__
-/* Native 4 KiB: two roots plus up to seven L2 pages per 6 GiB mapping.
+/* Native 4 KiB: two roots plus up to ten L2 pages per mapping of up to 9 GiB.
  * The physical and virtual bases may each straddle an extra 1 GiB region.
  */
-#define BOOTSTRAP_TABLE_SIZE (ARM_PGBYTES * 16)
+#define BOOTSTRAP_TABLE_SIZE (ARM_PGBYTES * 22)
 #else /* defined(ARM_LARGE_MEMORY) */
 #define BOOTSTRAP_TABLE_SIZE (ARM_PGBYTES * 8)
 #endif /* defined(ARM_LARGE_MEMORY) */
